OL,3,GNEWSA'Safety first' as wedding guests
OL,4,Astranded on island after Storm Boelo
OL,5,
OL,6,FGuests attending a wedding on Lower
OL,7,FLough Erne in a County Fermanagh island
OL,8,Fended up stranded after the ferry took
OL,9,Fon water during Storm Boelo.
OL,11,FAt the weekend, the storm saw gusts of
OL,12,Fwind reach almost 80mph in some areas
OL,13,Fand led to flights and ferries being
OL,14,Fcancelled.
OL,16,FGuest Shea Clarke, who was on Lusty Beg
OL,17,Fisland said that, despite the weather
OL,18,Fspirits were high, the staff were
OL,19,F"great and obviously it's too dangerous
OL,20,Fto cross and the boat can't cross so
OL,21,Fsafety comes first".
OL,23,APub: 26-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,413,410,260,120,0,100
